   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to reducing the dimensions of signs required to be displayed where wine ice cream is being sold",
    "basePrintNo": "S5823",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5823-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §200, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5823\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to\nreducing the dimensions of signs required to be displayed where wine\nice cream is being sold\n\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nAmends the opening paragraph of subparagraph (iii) of paragraph (a) of\nsubdivision 15 of section 200 of the agriculture and markets law to\nprovide that advisory signs to be displayed conspicuously at the point\nof sale of wine ice cream have to be a minimum of 7 inches by 5\ninches.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nSeeking to expand the opportunities of farms and agribusinesses the\nlegislature passed and the Governor signed legislation in 2008\n(chapter 189 of the laws of 2008) that provided for the regulated sale\nof wine ice cream. There were many provisions provided for in that law\nto ensure that only those twenty-one years of age and older would be\nable to purchase and consume this product.  This bill while reducing\nthe minimum sign requirement size slightly still ensures the growth of\nthis specialty agri-goodie while properly regulating it.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
